nty&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and March to April, April to May and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 27% of normal in September to October and 25% in October to November. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 31% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 12792 had its driest year in 1954 at 56% of normal.</p>"}
